= Introduction

This book tells the story of the families of Jory, Tamsin and Nora Penhallow, the children of David and Karin (Solberg) Penhallow of Madison, Wisconsin. The Penhallows are a sample family. They were invented to show how Flyleaf turns family records into a printed book and a private family website. The places and the history are real. The people, the records and the sources are not.

The book has two parts. *Part I — The Narrative* tells the family story branch by branch, ending with the present generation. *Part II — The Genealogical Register* lists each person with dates, places, spouses and children where known, and the sources for each. It is the place to look up a relationship or see where a detail in the story comes from.

Some of the story rests on original records. Other parts come from published histories, an online tree or family memories, and these are not all equally reliable. Where a name, date or relationship is uncertain, the text says so, and *Open Questions* gathers what is still unknown.

